## Headline

The task prompt asks to enforce a three-ID contract: `signal_id` / `execution_intent_id` / `shadow_decision_id`. Two of those IDs are canonical, one is not. `shadow_decision_id` is **not** a field of the V2 canonical lineage chain (`LineageBlock` §1.3.1, 12B closure) and is **explicitly disallowed** by three runtime/projection harnesses. Enforcement cannot land without a prior upstream contract amendment.

## Canonical chain (six fields, not three)

`v2/backend/app/api/schemas/lineage.py:33-51` — `LineageBlock` with `extra="forbid"`:
```
feature_snapshot_id, prediction_id, signal_id, decision_id,
risk_decision_id, execution_intent_id (+ lineage_gap_reason)
```
No `shadow_decision_id`.

## Blockers (each with exact evidence pointer)

| # | Severity | Blocker | Evidence pointer |
|---|---|---|---|
| 001 | HIGH | `shadow_decision_id` not in canonical `LineageBlock`; pydantic `extra="forbid"` rejects it | `v2/backend/app/api/schemas/lineage.py:26-51` |
| 002 | HIGH | Shadow Mode Evidence Collection harness lists `shadow_decision_id` AND `execution_intent_id` in `DISALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES` | `v2/backend/tests/unit/shadow_mode_evidence_collection_harness/test_shadow_mode_evidence_collection_harness.py:55-58,194-199` |
| 003 | HIGH | `PaperLedgerExplainabilityEnvelope.FORBIDDEN_ENVELOPE_FIELDS` includes both `shadow_decision_id` and `execution_intent_id`; envelope also omits `signal_id` | `v2/backend/tests/unit/decision_explainability_paper_ledger_projection/test_decision_explainability_paper_ledger_projection.py:40-77,180-184` |
| 004 | HIGH | Historical PnL replay wiring forbids `shadow_decision_id` | `v2/backend/tests/unit/historical_pnl_replay_wiring/test_historical_pnl_replay_wiring.py:147` |
| 005 | HIGH | No runtime writer for `shadow_decision_id` — only two static proof-scenario `@property` getters | `v2/backend/app/proof/non_live_operational_proof.py:77-79`; `v2/backend/app/proof/historical_30d_replay_and_paper_proof.py:76-77` |
| 006 | MED | `LineageValidatorMiddleware` is a documented scaffold passthrough; nine §9.1 validators not implemented | `v2/backend/app/api/middleware/lineage_validator.py:1-21` |
| 007 | MED | Frontend `LineageBlock.intent_id` vs backend `execution_intent_id`; frontend adds 3 non-canonical fields | `v2/frontend/src/lineage/block.tsx:1-12` vs `v2/backend/app/api/schemas/lineage.py:26-51` |
| 008 | MED | Paper runtime emits `orchestrator_decision_id`; canonical schema uses `decision_id` | `v2/backend/app/services/signal_publisher.py:271,373-380`; `v2/frontend/src/pages/paper-trading/index.tsx:36` |
| 009 | MED | Paper ledger projection envelope omits `signal_id` even though `signal_id` is canonical | `v2/backend/tests/unit/decision_explainability_paper_ledger_projection/test_decision_explainability_paper_ledger_projection.py:40-56` |

## ID writers (signal / execution_intent / shadow_decision)

- `signal_id`: produced at `v2/backend/app/services/signal_publisher.py:108-112` (canonical `sig_<sha256[:12]>`); also at `signal_publisher.py:267-269` (`sig_{tick_id}` paper runtime) and `v2/backend/app/cli/live_observer_bridge.py:478` (shadow-twin fallback).
- `execution_intent_id`: `signal_publisher.py:273,351-363` (`pei_{tick_id}`) and `live_observer_bridge.py:476,540-547` (`shadow_intent_{epoch_ms}`).
- `shadow_decision_id`: **no runtime writer**. Only `non_live_operational_proof.py:77-79` and `historical_30d_replay_and_paper_proof.py:76-77`, both `@property` derivations on static proof scenarios.

## Dashboard projection parity (FAILING)

Expected canonical chain: `feature_snapshot_id, prediction_id, signal_id, decision_id, risk_decision_id, execution_intent_id`.

- Paper Trading page (`v2/frontend/src/pages/paper-trading/index.tsx:33-38`) — uses `orchestrator_decision_id` instead of `decision_id`. Missing canonical-name parity.
- `LineageBlockView` (`v2/frontend/src/lineage/block.tsx:1-12,18-28`) — uses `intent_id` instead of `execution_intent_id`; includes 3 fields (`model_version`, `checkpoint_id`, `config_version`) that are not in the backend `LineageBlock`.
- `PaperLedgerExplainabilityEnvelope` (test_decision_explainability_paper_ledger_projection.py:40-56) — has `decision_id, risk_decision_id, prediction_id, feature_snapshot_id, paper_trade_id`. Omits `signal_id`. Forbids `execution_intent_id` and `shadow_decision_id`.

## Required next actions (cannot self-execute)

1. **Author a 12B §1.3.1 contract-amendment proposal** that picks one path:
   - Path A (recommended): drop `shadow_decision_id` from the enforcement prompt and enforce the existing six canonical IDs. Aligns with current schema + harness contracts. Zero churn.
   - Path B: extend `LineageBlock` with a seventh `shadow_decision_id` field, then update `DISALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES`, `FORBIDDEN_ENVELOPE_FIELDS`, and the historical-replay forbid list, plus introduce a runtime writer in the shadow-twin path of `live_observer_bridge.py`. High churn — requires updating ≥4 harnesses and the projection envelope.
2. Reconcile name drift: rename frontend `intent_id` → `execution_intent_id`; rename paper runtime `orchestrator_decision_id` → `decision_id` (or declare an alias inside `LineageBlock`).
3. Implement the nine §9.1 validators in `LineageValidatorMiddleware` only after the contract is final.
4. Extend `PaperLedgerExplainabilityEnvelope` to include `signal_id` (and `execution_intent_id` if Path B is chosen).

## GO / NO-GO

**NO-GO.** Enforcement cannot proceed without an amendment to `v2/backend/app/api/schemas/lineage.py:26-51` and the four forbid-lists referenced above. Any code change that adds `shadow_decision_id` to a runtime payload today will break tests `test_harness_no_shadow_decision_id_field_introduced`, `test_envelope_has_only_allowed_projection_fields`, and the historical-replay wiring assertion at line 147.

